            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is explicitly [out of scope of 'mini.files' itself](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/5495dd5480843148b0e9ed57b42d32ea47ac2b52/doc/mini-files.txt#L35-L37). Integration with 'lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim' does not make much sense (as it is intended to show information for files that are actually on disk, not for \"scratch\" buffers), but showing Git status next to the file system entry should be possible. For example, take look at [this gist](https://gist.github.com/bassamsdata/eec0a3065152226581f8d4244cce9051#file-notes-md).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This is explicitly <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/5495dd5480843148b0e9ed57b42d32ea47ac2b52/doc/mini-files.txt#L35-L37\">out of scope of 'mini.files' itself</a>. Integration with 'lewis6991/gitsigns.nvim' does not make much sense (as it is intended to show information for files that are actually on disk, not for \"scratch\" buffers), but showing Git status next to the file system entry should be possible. For example, take look at <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/bassamsdata/eec0a3065152226581f8d4244cce9051#file-notes-md\">this gist</a>.</p>",
